<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">4.The Co holds strategic investments in the grp and JV entities that are engaged primarily in mfg of components and providing technological services for the transportation industry, mainly the automotive sector.The Co also provides mgmt, IT and BD services to its subsidiaries and JV entities.   6.Share of L and L of JV entities disclosed in the consol FR includes the share of exceptional expenditure, recorded by RNSS Rs 2,254 L for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31, 21,  Rs NIL for the qtr ended Sep 30, 21 Rs 2,416 Lakhs for the qtr ended Dec 31 20 and Rs 3,435 Lakhs for nine months ended Dec 31, 20 and Rs 8,678 Lakhs for the yr ended Mar 31, 21. This exceptional expenditure was incurred by RNSS towards incremental warranty claims with respect to certain specific lots of products sold by RNSS to one of its customers. RNSS has determined the amt based on technical estimates and is currently in discussions with various parties to determine and conclude on certain aspects that may impact the quantum of the warranty liability. Based on its assessment and pending final outcome of such discussions and negotiations, RNSS believes that the provision carried by them as at Dec 31, 21 is adequate.   7. Exceptional items in the above financial results includes the following:   a.In respect of Rt4u, the Co had assessed the carrying value of its investments and considered the fair value changes thereto resulting in a reduction in the carrying value aggregating to Rs. 1,781 Lakhs for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31, 21 and Rs. 1,557 Lakhs for the year ended Mar 31, 21 being shown as an exceptional charge in the Stand FR; and the corresponding effect in the Consol FR towards impairment of goodwill was Rs. 162 Lakhs for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31 21.   b. REVL incurred VRS expenditure of Rs. 265 Lakhs and Rs. 355 Lakhs for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31 21 Rs. 46 Lakhs and Rs. 127 Lakhs for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31, 20 and Rs. 90 Lakhs and Rs.172 Lakhs for the qtr ended Sep 30, 21 and yr ended Mar 31 21. Further, REVL made a Profit on sale of Land of Rs. 2,395 Lakhs for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31 20 and for the yr ended Mar 31 21.   c. LMCA was entitled to certain economic relief provided by the U.S. govt in order to manage the impact of COVID-19 pandemic. Pursuant to such economic relief schemes, during the nine months ended Dec 31 21, LMCA received an approval for forgiveness of the PPP Loan from the U.S. SBA for an amt of USD 2.63 million (INR 1,945 Lakhs). Further, LMCA was eligible for ERC from the U.S. IRS during the nine months ended Dec 31 21 for an amt of USD 3.66 million (INR 2,726 Lakhs) (including USD 1.26 million (INR 950 Lakhs) for the qtr ended Dec 31 21 and USD 1.23 million (INR 914 Lakhs) for the qtr ended Sep 30, 21). The aggregate amts of such relief have been recorded as an exceptional income in the consol results for the qtr ended Sept 30,21 and for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31 21.   8.During the qtr ended Dec 31 21, the Co's board approved the divestment of 87,383 (nos.) equity shares representing 1% of the total shareholding in RTSS for a consideration of Rs. 2,016 Lakhs. Pursuant to this divestment, the Co holds 49% and ZF holds the remaining 51% shareholding in the RTSS.   9.Subsequent to the qtr ended Dec 31 21, the Co acquired 8,49,979 equity shares of Rs.10 each fully paid up in RML on Jan 11 22 pursuant to conversion of 8,49,979 warrants for an aggregate consideration of Rs. 2,000 lakhs (including the warrant exercise price of Rs. 1,500 Lakhs). Pursuant to such acquisition, the shareholding of the Co in RML will stand at 71.77 %.   11.During the yr ended Mar 31 21, the Co had opted to settle its pending IT litigations for certain AYs under the Vivad Se Vishwas scheme. In view of this, the Co had created a provision of Rs. 733 Lakhs towards IT in respect of earlier yrs which has been disclosed separately under the head tax expenses for the yr ended Mar 31 21.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
